<title>INDIA: India 96/97 sugar output seen at 13 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 sugar output seen at 13 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's sugar output in the 1996/97 (October-September) season is expected to fall to 13 million tonnes from 16.5 million in the previous year, Agriculture Minister Chaturanan Mishra said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The output is expected to fall because some crop diversion has taken place,&quot; Mishra told reporters in the Indian capital.</p>
<p>&quot;But we don't have to worry because we have sufficient carry-over stocks.&quot;</p>
<p>Mishra said India produced 12.1 million tonnes of sugar between October 1996 and April 1997, compared with 13.8 million in the corresponding period in 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
